From c57325f64dc2d8a5e8d82cb6976197039fc2e4af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilPatrick06 <187923600+EvilPatrick06@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:37:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(desktop): a stored session the store already owns is
 read on that owner, not walked across the active source's profiles

probeStoredSession took an owner only from its caller. resolveSessionProfile
and the other profile-only callers name none, so a session whose exact owner
the store already knew (tile route, unique hint, tagged row or proven runtime
event) still went down the cross-profile ladder. That ladder walks $profiles,
the ACTIVE source's names. On a remote-primary Desktop, This device's Bot Chat
was looked up under every remote Bot's name, and the session read pin sent each
lookup to the owner's connection ('local'), which refused each name it does not
have ("Profile \"rift\" no longer exists") and held one lookup 120 s on a
remote-dashboard dial.

The probe now starts from the same sync owner ladder session RPCs use, and an
exact route found there is fail-closed like an explicit one. A session with no
known exact owner walks the profiles as before.
